# Force LF regardless of the checking-out machine's core.autocrlf. Several
# of these files are built into (or executed inside) Linux containers --
# shell scripts with CRLF line endings fail there (a CRLF shebang line does
# not match `#!/usr/bin/env bash`), and Windows checkouts default
# core.autocrlf to true, which would otherwise silently corrupt them.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
